```julia
@time sum(abs2.(rand(10^6)));
```

On 1.13 the line looks like `0.007 seconds (6 allocations: 15.259 MiB, 52% gc time)`. The pieces: number of heap allocations, total bytes allocated (not peak), and the share of wall time spent in garbage collection. A high GC percentage means the call produces lots of garbage, so the fix is to allocate less (preallocate, fuse, use views), not to tune the GC. Run it twice and read the second line; the first includes compilation.
